==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbɔːt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbɔɹt/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abort.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)t|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃er-}}
From {{der|en|enm|-}}, from {{der|en|la|abortus}}, perfect active participle of {{m|la|aborior||miscarry}}, formed from {{m|la|ab}} + {{m|la|orior||come into being}}. {{doublet|en|abortus}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|military|aeronautics}} An early termination of a mission, action, or procedure in relation to missiles or spacecraft; the craft making such a mission.
#: {{ux|en|We've had '''aborts''' on three of our last seven launches.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} The [[function]] used to abort a [[process]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} An [[event]] in which a process is aborted.
#: {{ux|en|We've had three '''aborts''' over the last two days.}}
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} The [[product]] of a miscarriage; an [[aborted]] offspring; an [[abortion]]. {{defdate|First attested in the early 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[miscarriage]]; an [[untimely]] birth; an [[abortion]]. {{defdate|Attested from around (1350 to 1470) until the mid 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|part=I|section=2|member=4|subsection=vi|passage=In Japonia 'tis a common thing to stifle their children if they be poor, or to make an '''abort''', which Aristotle commends.}}

